## Review & Understand
- **Goal:** Add charts to the Infrastructure view giving a quick view of **performance** and **possible problems**.
- **Reuse:** same chart library as `DailyChart.vue` → `chart.js/auto` (already wrapped by the existing `MonitoringChart.vue`).
- **Foundation in place:** `useInfraMonitor.js` (live by default, 5s default cadence, rolling 120-sample buffer) + `MonitoringChart.vue`. Missing: the panel, and the wiring in `InfraView.vue`.

## Change summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/views/infra/MonitoringPanel.vue` | **new** — 3 time-series charts (host load / container states / docker resources), window KPI tiles (now + peak + avg), a rule-based **"Possible problems"** list and the **busiest containers** ranking (click → existing drawer). |
| `src/views/infra/InfraView.vue` | **update** — `Monitoring` tab first in the strip (badge = collected samples), refresh-interval selector next to the Live switch (both driven by the monitor), filter bar hidden on that route, `startMonitoring()` on mount / `stopMonitoring()` on unmount. |

`useInfraMonitor.js` and `MonitoringChart.vue` are used **as-is** — no changes needed there.

