## Notes

- **Same library, same look:** all three charts go through `MonitoringChart.vue` → `chart.js/auto` with the palette/typography of `DailyChart.vue` (`#e5e7eb` / `#9ca3af` / `#374151` / `rgba(55,65,81,.25)`), `animation:false` so a 5s poll never fights the canvas.
- **Honest data:** the Docker API only exposes a snapshot, so every refresh appends one point to a 120-sample ring buffer (`useInfraMonitor.js`). Nothing is interpolated; "Clear" empties the window.
- **Performance signals:** CPU / Memory / Disk (%) + Containers by state (running, restarting, unhealthy, stopped) + Docker resources (images, volumes, networks — spots volume/image leaks).
- **Problem signals:** thresholds (80/90 %), `health === 'unhealthy'`, `restart_count >= 5` crash loops, stuck `restarting`, stopped containers pinning images; sorted error → warning → info.
- **Accessibility:** the interval `<select>` has `aria-label`, tabs keep `role="tab"`, every issue row pairs colour with an icon + text, progress meters carry the numeric value.
- **Single poller:** the header switch/selector now drive `useInfraMonitor` (`setLive` / `setRefreshInterval`), so `useInfra.toggleLive`'s fixed 5s timer is no longer started from this view — no double polling.

